hermes v0.23.0: OpenRouter `:batch` models are never offered or used for chat.

`<model>:batch` ids are OpenRouter's asynchronous Batch API (results
within a 24 h window, no streaming), unusable for an interactive agent.
With model_catalog.openrouter_all_models they made up 67 of the 368 rows
of the OpenRouter picker and sat right next to the real model under the
same display name (deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 and
deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017:batch both read "DeepSeek V4.1 Flash
1017"), so the chat model looked missing behind its batch twin.

- catalog: fetch_openrouter_models drops them (model_ids,
  provider_model_ids, /api/model/options and model.options, TUI and
  messaging /model, `hermes model`), and drop_unofferable_model_ids
  drops them from every OpenRouter-routed picker row (is_openrouter_route:
  provider openrouter, an openrouter.ai base_url, or a named custom
  provider pointing there). _credential_fingerprint("openrouter") gains a
  marker so provider_models_cache.json rows cached with them are refetched.
- resolution: an OpenRouter `...:batch` model runs as the same id without
  `:batch`, logged as a WARNING, in init_agent (every AIAgent: main,
  delegated children, cron) and its fallback chain, agent switch_model,
  model_switch.switch_model (/model), bind_route_entry (fallback
  activation) and resolve_provider_client (auxiliary clients).

Applies after hermes-openrouter-exclude-native.patch (extends its
filter_catalog / drop_unofferable_model_ids lines).
Tests: the offline check hyperhermes/checks/openrouter-no-batch.
Upstream status: not reported; hyperhermes-only.

